Timer thread: timers ordered by a copy of what osSetTimer was given, removed by address (upstream orders its set by
the timestamp read from the OSTimer in game memory; a stack timer stopped late and its memory reused corrupted the set,
and timers stopped firing: a game hung in a sleep). Found in another port on 2026-10-17.

diff --git i/ultramodern/src/timer.cpp w/ultramodern/src/timer.cpp
